-- netFORUM Enterprise: the session token comes from the Authenticate RESPONSE HEADER, and the
-- objects whose default column list cannot carry their watermark now declare one.
--
-- 1. THE TOKEN WAS READ FROM THE WRONG ELEMENT. Through connector 1.3.4, Authenticate() read the token
--    from the body's <AuthenticateResult>. On a real tenant that element holds the namespace URI
--    "http://www.avectra.com/2005/" — the token is in the SOAP RESPONSE HEADER,
--    <soap:Header><AuthorizationToken><Token>, which the WSDL declares as an OUTPUT header of the
--    Authenticate operation. The connector therefore sent the URI as its token, and netFORUM answers an
--    unrecognised token with HTTP 500 + faultstring "Locked" on EVERY call — with nothing locked.
--    Vendor-confirmed with a captured Authenticate response, 2026-09-15. Connector 1.3.4's changelog
--    attributed "Locked" to MethodsFaultLimitPerDay; that diagnosis was wrong.
--    Integration.Configuration.AuthFlowNote / TokenRefreshStrategyNote and CredentialType.Description
--    said "the token is the AuthenticateResult string" — operator-facing text served from the tenant
--    catalog — so they are corrected here. FieldSchema is unchanged (it never named the element).
--
-- 2. THE DEFAULT COLUMN LIST NEVER CARRIES THE WATERMARK. With an empty szColumnList (the documented
--    form — '*' is invalid) GetQuery returns the tenant's DEFAULT list columns, and on a live tenant not
--    one of the 23 incremental objects' default lists includes its <prefix>_change_date column, so
--    incremental sync could never advance. Three objects (IndividualPhone, IndividualFax,
--    InvoiceDetailCustomer) fault even on the empty list because their default list is itself '*'.
--    Naming the columns works — including the watermark, an incremental ">=" predicate on it, and
--    ORDER BY it — so each object whose list was PROVEN live declares Configuration.columnList
--    (its default columns plus the watermark, minus display columns the door refuses by name);
--    the connector (>= 1.3.6) sends a declared list and completes it with the PK, ordering key and
--    watermark. Objects with no proven list keep the empty list and the WATERMARK_COLUMN_ABSENT warning.
--    Each object's columnListNote records its provenance. DeclaredAgainst.catalogLastEditedAt → 2026-09-15.
--
-- Delta only: no rows are inserted or deleted, no IDs re-minted. Generated from the metadata JSON.
-- PostgreSQL twin, hand-authored from the same metadata (the SS->PG converter is not needed for plain UPDATEs).

CREATE EXTENSION IF NOT EXISTS "pgcrypto";
CREATE EXTENSION IF NOT EXISTS "uuid-ossp";
CREATE SCHEMA IF NOT EXISTS __mj;
SET search_path TO __mj, public;
SET standard_conforming_strings = on;

UPDATE "__mj"."Integration"
SET "Configuration" = '{"AuthFlow":"two-step","AuthFlowNote":"netFORUM Enterprise xWeb uses a two-step SOAP session-token model. Step 1 (bootstrap): POST a SOAP Authenticate(userName, password) envelope to <tenantBaseURL>/xweb/secure/netForumXML.asmx with SOAPAction http://www.avectra.com/2005/Authenticate. The credentials travel as ELEMENTS IN THE SOAP BODY — there is no HTTP Basic Authorization header on this call — and the envelope deliberately carries no AuthorizationToken header, because it is the bootstrap. The token is in the SOAP RESPONSE HEADER — <soap:Header><AuthorizationToken><Token> — which the WSDL declares as an output header of Authenticate. The body''s AuthenticateResult is NOT the token: on a real tenant it holds the namespace URI http://www.avectra.com/2005/. CORRECTED 2026-09-15: this note previously said the token was the AuthenticateResult string, and the connector read it that way through 1.3.4, so it sent that URI as its token; netFORUM answers an unrecognised token with HTTP 500 + faultstring ''Locked'' on every call, with nothing locked. Vendor-confirmed with a captured Authenticate response. Do not restore the AuthenticateResult wording. Step 2: every subsequent xWeb call carries that token in a SOAP <AuthorizationToken><Token> HEADER ELEMENT. CORRECTED 2026-08-26: this note previously described a JSON shim at /xWeb/JSON/Authenticate using HTTP Basic to mint an Authorization: Bearer token. The connector has never done that on this code path and its own header comment states the opposite verbatim (''Auth (TWO-STEP, SOAP — NOT HTTP Basic / WWW-Authenticate / Bearer)''). Do not restore the Basic/Bearer wording. Source: connector code — NetForumConnector.Authenticate(), BuildSoapEnvelope(), SoapHeaders() (cited by SYMBOL, not line number: the previous note cited ''NetForumConnector.ts:326-357'', which drifted onto unrelated code). Token validity window is not published by the vendor; the connector assumes a 1-hour TTL (TOKEN_TTL_MS) and re-authenticates on 401.","AuthHeaderPattern":"<AuthorizationToken xmlns=\"http://www.avectra.com/2005/\"><Token>{token}</Token></AuthorizationToken>","AuthHeaderPatternNote":"NOT an HTTP header. The session token is a SOAP HEADER ELEMENT inside <soap:Header>, namespaced to http://www.avectra.com/2005/. The only HTTP headers the connector sets are Content-Type: text/xml; charset=utf-8 and SOAPAction: http://www.avectra.com/2005/<MethodName>. CORRECTED 2026-08-26 from ''Authorization: Bearer <token>'', which described a transport this connector does not use. Source: connector code — NetForumConnector.Authenticate(), BuildSoapEnvelope(), SoapHeaders() (cited by SYMBOL, not line number: the previous note cited ''NetForumConnector.ts:326-357'', which drifted onto unrelated code).","TransportMode":"soap","TransportModeNote":"The connector speaks SOAP 1.1 over HTTPS to netFORUMXML.asmx exclusively — one endpoint path (/xweb/secure/netForumXML.asmx, DEFAULT_SOAP_PATH), overridable per object via IntegrationObject.Configuration.soapEndpoint. The WSDL is the authoritative contract. CORRECTED 2026-08-26 from ''soap_with_json_shim'': a JSON shim at /xWeb/JSON/<MethodName> is described in vendor-adjacent material, but this connector does not call it and its existence has NOT been verified against a live tenant from this repo — so the declared TransportMode now states what the code actually does rather than an unexercised alternative. Source: connector code — NetForumConnector.Authenticate(), BuildSoapEnvelope(), SoapHeaders() (cited by SYMBOL, not line number: the previous note cited ''NetForumConnector.ts:326-357'', which drifted onto unrelated code).","SOAPNamespace":"http://www.avectra.com/2005/","SOAPNamespaceNote":"Avectra-era namespace retained by Community Brands. All WSDL operations and DataObjectType schemas use this namespace. Source: WSDL namespace declaration confirmed on both ASM (myasm.asm.org) and APCO (apconetforum.org) public instances.","NavigationBaseURLNote":"The xWeb endpoint is per-tenant. There is no single canonical host. The shape is: <tenantHost>/xWeb/secure/netFORUMXML.asmx (SOAP) or <tenantHost>/xWeb/JSON/<MethodName> (JSON shim). The BaseURL is stored in the per-CompanyIntegration credential (netforum-token.schema.json.BaseURL field). Source: credential schema + connector code ParseConfig() method + public WSDL endpoints (myasm.asm.org/xweb/secure/netforumxml.asmx, apconetforum.org/xweb/secure/netFORUMXML.asmx) confirming the path shape.","route":"netforum_enterprise_xweb","routeNote":"Disambiguates this connector from netFORUM Pro (different product with different API surface) and from the Higher Logic XML route. This connector targets netFORUM Enterprise via xWeb only. Source: SOURCE_STUDY.md Scope Decision + NetForumContext.md route taxonomy.","PaginationDefaults":{"type":"None","description":"xWeb GetQuery returns the full result set in a single call — there is no standard offset/limit/cursor pagination in the API protocol. The DataGrid row limit (see xWebDataGridRowLimitBehavior) is a server-side cap that TRUNCATES results silently when the result set exceeds the configured maximum. The connector must detect truncation (compare returned row count to the row limit) and split queries via date-range partitioning or other filters rather than assuming completeness. The PaginationType=None reflects the API protocol; the row-limit truncation is a separate concern documented in xWebDataGridRowLimitBehavior.","xWebDataGridRowLimitBehavior":"The xWeb DataGrid row limit is a configurable server-side ceiling on the number of rows returned by a single GetQuery call. Default is approximately 100-200 rows on older installations; some installations set it as high as 1000+. The exact limit is customer-configured in iWeb and is NOT discoverable via a credential-free API call. Behavior when the limit is hit: the response is silently truncated to the limit — the API does NOT return a pagination cursor, a \"hasMore\" flag, or any error. The connector MUST treat a response whose row count exactly equals a round-number boundary (e.g., exactly 100, 200, 500, 1000) as a potential truncation signal and implement date-range partitioning or object-specific szWhereClause filters to obtain the complete dataset. Source: SOURCE_STUDY.md Gaps section (\"Row limit configuration ... customer-configured and not in the public WSDL. Only discoverable via sandbox testing.\"); Abila docs GetQuery page (documentation.abila.com) mentions \"@TOP N\" modifier for GetQuery object names (e.g., \"Individual @TOP -1\" for all rows, \"Individual @TOP 5000\" for a bounded count). The \"@TOP -1\" modifier in the szObjectName parameter bypasses the DataGrid row limit. EvidenceStrength: ImpliedFromExample.","getTotalViaTopMinusOne":"Use the szObjectName \"@TOP -1\" suffix (e.g., szObjectName=\"Individual @TOP -1\") in GetQuery to bypass the DataGrid row limit and retrieve all records. Note: this may be slow on large datasets. Alternatively use \"@TOP N\" for incremental batching by date range. Source: Abila docs GetQuery.htm (documentation.abila.com/netforum-enterprise/2017.1/Content/xWeb/Methods/GetQuery.htm)."},"IncrementalSyncCapability":true,"IncrementalSyncDescription":"NetForum xWeb supports incremental sync via the szWhereClause parameter on GetQuery. Each facade entity has its own prefixed last-modified timestamp column (e.g., ind_last_updated_dt for Individual, evt_last_updated_dt for Event). There is no universal watermark field name — the prefix varies per entity (ind_, evt_, reg_, cmt_, cmm_, etc.). The connector resolves the object-specific watermark column via the WSDL DataObjectType field names. Source: connector code (ResolveWatermarkColumn + ResolveDeclaredWatermarkColumn methods; NF_OBJECTS catalog listing ind_last_updated_dt, evt_start_dt per object). WSDL evidence: DateTime-typed fields ending in _dt present in Individual_*, EventsRegistrant_*, etc. DataObjectType schemas.","IncrementalWatermarkFieldPattern":"<prefix>_last_updated_dt","IncrementalWatermarkFieldPatternNote":"Each facade entity uses a prefixed last-updated column. Examples from the static catalog: ind_last_updated_dt (Individual), and per-type inference for others. The prefix matches the entity''s column naming convention (ind_ = Individual, evt_ = EventsRegistrant, org_ = Organization, etc.). Source: connector NF_OBJECTS catalog + WSDL DataObjectType analysis. No single universal field name exists across all objects.","WebhooksAvailable":false,"WebhooksNote":"NetForum Enterprise xWeb has no webhook or change-data-capture endpoint. The API is pull-based (GetQuery + incremental watermark). The connector comment in NetForumConnector.ts explicitly states: \"Webhooks (NOT available) — no webhook/CDC support in NetForum\". Source: connector code comment (Line 40: \"Webhooks (NOT available)\"); absence from WSDL (277 operations; none are subscription/push endpoints). EvidenceStrength: ImpliedFromExample (comprehensive absence from the WSDL is strong implied evidence).","BulkOperationsAvailable":false,"BulkOperationsNote":"No batch/bulk mutation endpoint in xWeb. CRUD is per-record via InsertFacadeObject / UpdateFacadeObject. The WEBCentralizedShoppingCart* cluster (124 operations) handles multi-line-item order entry but these are transient cart operations, not bulk record mutation. Source: WSDL operation analysis (277 ops; no batch create/update endpoints). EvidenceStrength: ImpliedFromExample.","APIVersioningStrategy":"none","APIVersioningStrategyNote":"xWeb does not use URL-path versioning. The SOAP namespace http://www.avectra.com/2005/ encodes the Avectra-era year but is not versioned in the URL path. The WSDL endpoint is /xweb/secure/netforumxml.asmx?WSDL with no version segment. Backward compatibility is maintained across Community Brands releases by adding new operations without removing or changing existing ones. Source: WSDL URL patterns on public instances (myasm.asm.org, apconetforum.org). EvidenceStrength: ImpliedFromExample.","TokenRefreshStrategy":"session-token-reissue","TokenRefreshStrategyNote":"There is no OAuth2-style refresh_token. When the session token expires, the connector re-authenticates from scratch with the same SOAP Authenticate(userName, password) envelope (credentials as body elements, not HTTP Basic) and reads the new token from the SOAP response header (<AuthorizationToken><Token>). It keeps a token cache with a 1-hour TTL (TOKEN_TTL_MS) and re-authenticates before it elapses; a 401 on any call clears the cache and retries once. CORRECTED 2026-09-15: this note previously described a /xWeb/JSON/Authenticate call with stored Basic credentials — a transport this connector does not use — and cited line numbers that had drifted onto unrelated code. Source: connector code — NetForumConnector.Authenticate(), ParseAuthenticateToken(), MakeRawHTTPRequest() (cited by SYMBOL).","ErrorResponseShape":{"description":"NetForum xWeb JSON mode returns HTTP 4xx/5xx with error details in various forms depending on the endpoint and xWeb version. Common patterns: (1) SOAP fault wrapped in JSON; (2) {\"ExceptionMessage\": \"...\", \"ExceptionType\": \"...\", \"Message\": \"...\"} for .NET-style errors; (3) Plain HTTP status codes with no body for auth failures. SOAP mode returns standard SOAP Fault elements. The connector handles non-200 responses by inspecting status codes and surfacing the raw body. Source: connector code MakeHTTPRequest error handling; EvidenceStrength: ImpliedFromExample (inferred from .NET/SOAP stack patterns; exact shapes require sandbox verification).","soapFaultElements":["faultcode","faultstring","detail"],"dotNetExceptionFields":["ExceptionMessage","ExceptionType","Message","StackTrace"],"authErrorStatus":401,"rateLimitStatus":429},"WriteCapability":{"Create":true,"Update":true,"Delete":"unconfirmed","description":"InsertFacadeObject and UpdateFacadeObject are documented in the WSDL (ExplicitStatement). DeleteFacadeObject appears in the WSDL as an operation name but is NOT confirmed in any reachable vendor documentation page. The connector sets SupportsDelete=false and routes DeleteRecord to a best-effort call that returns an error rather than silently claiming success. The vendor appears to prefer \"soft delete\" via status flags. Source: connector code comment lines 143-147 (\"Vendor docs document InsertFacadeObject + UpdateFacadeObject; no DeleteFacadeObject appears in any reachable doc page ... Keeping the flag false until DeleteFacadeObject is confirmed\"). WSDL evidence for Create/Update: InsertFacadeObject, UpdateFacadeObject operations present (ExplicitStatement).","CreateMethod":"InsertFacadeObject (JSON: POST /xWeb/JSON/InsertFacadeObject)","UpdateMethod":"UpdateFacadeObject (JSON: POST /xWeb/JSON/UpdateFacadeObject)","DeleteMethod":"DeleteFacadeObject (UNCONFIRMED — connector returns error)","WritePathNote":"All mutations route through the FacadeObject generic interface. Entity-specific WEB* operations (e.g., WEBIndividualInsert, WEBOrganizationInsert, WEBContactRequestInsert) exist in the WSDL for a subset of entities but the connector uses InsertFacadeObject as the universal Create path. The FacadeObject interface accepts szObjectName + oRecord parameters."},"ConcurrencyControl":"none","ConcurrencyControlNote":"xWeb exposes no ETag, If-Match, version counter, or optimistic-lock header on GetFacadeObject or UpdateFacadeObject responses. The API is last-write-wins. Conflict handling relies on snapshot-3-way diff at the MJ sync layer, not on vendor-side locking. Source: WSDL operation analysis (no ETag/version fields in DataObjectType schemas); connector code (no If-Match header sent). EvidenceStrength: ImpliedFromExample.","DeleteSemantics":"soft","DeleteSemanticsNote":"NetForum uses status flags rather than hard record deletion for most entities. The connector comment explicitly notes: \"NetForum more commonly uses status flags (soft delete) rather than hard delete\" (NetForumConnector.ts line 145-146). The specific status flag name varies by entity type (e.g., active/inactive flag in Individual, Membership status fields). Hard delete via DeleteFacadeObject is unconfirmed from documentation. Source: connector code comments; EvidenceStrength: ImpliedFromExample.","DeleteStatusFlagNote":"The soft-delete field name varies per entity type. Exact field names for each entity require sandbox verification. Common patterns in AMS systems include: active_flag, status_code, or equivalent. The WSDL DataObjectType schemas contain boolean/status fields but the specific \"deleted\" indicator is installation-dependent.","DefaultSyncDirection":"Pull","DefaultSyncDirectionNote":"Read-only by default. Write capability (InsertFacadeObject / UpdateFacadeObject) is confirmed in the WSDL but bidirectional sync must be explicitly validated against a customer sandbox before enabling. No ETag/version concurrency control exists, making conflict resolution purely snapshot-based. Source: provable-only discipline; connector SupportsDelete=false.","DefaultConflictResolution":"DestWins","DefaultConflictResolutionNote":"No ETag or version field in xWeb responses precludes MostRecent-based conflict resolution. DestWins (the external system wins) is the safer default for an AMS system where the source of record is the vendor. If bidirectional is enabled, manual review may be preferred for membership-critical fields. Source: ConcurrencyControl=none (no version field → cannot reliably determine which change is most recent).","universalPK":{"fieldName":"<entity_prefix>_<entity_abbreviation>_key","pattern":"Each NetForum facade entity has a GUID primary key named with the entity prefix and abbreviation (e.g., ind_cst_key for Individual, org_cst_key for Organization, mbr_key for Membership, evt_key for Event, reg_key for EventRegistration). The key is always a GUID string. The naming convention is <table_abbreviation>_key or <parent_abbreviation>_cst_key. Source: connector NF_OBJECTS catalog + WSDL DataObjectType schemas. Note: unlike REST APIs with a universal \"id\" field, netFORUM uses entity-specific key names.","examples":{"Individual":"ind_cst_key","Organization":"org_cst_key","Membership":"mbr_key","Event":"evt_key","EventRegistration":"reg_key","Committee":"cmt_key","CommitteeMember":"cmm_key","Invoice":"inv_key","Payment":"pmt_key","Product":"prd_key","Order":"ord_key","Donation":"don_key","Address":"adr_key","Session":"ses_key","Subscription":"sub_key","Certification":"crt_key","ContinuingEducation":"ceu_key"},"note":"The runtime SoftPKClassifier should look for the <entity>_key or <entity>_cst_key pattern. The _cst_key suffix indicates a Customer Key (customer GUID) which is the FK shared across Individual and Organization."},"RuntimeDiscoveryMechanism":{"CustomerQueries":"GetQueryDefinition(szObjectName) returns the underlying SQL join structure (obj_key, obj_name, obj_description, ListTable, ListFromTables elements). Call with each customer-specific query name to discover its schema. Requires authentication.","CustomerViews":"ExecuteMethod(szMethodName) can call customer-installed stored procedures and views. The method names are customer/partner-specific and must be discovered via customer documentation or admin questionnaire.","CustomColumns":"GetFacadeXMLSchema(szObjectName) returns the XSD schema for a facade object including custom fields added by the customer. Requires authentication.","HigherLogicStoredProcs":"HigherLogic-specific stored procedures (HigherLogic_GetChangedMembers, HigherLogic_GetMemberInfo, HigherLogic_GetChangedMeetings) are callable via ExecuteMethod only when the HL integration is installed. Presence is detected at connection time, not declared as static metadata."},"OutOfScopeObjectFamilies":["HigherLogic partner stored procedures (HigherLogic_GetChangedMembers, HigherLogic_GetMemberInfo, HigherLogic_GetChangedMeetings) — partner-installed, runtime-Discovered only","Custom customer query objects via GetQuery — customer-installation-specific, runtime-Discovered","Customer-specific SQL views via ExecuteMethod — installation-specific","Custom WEB* methods from customer extension WSDL files (e.g. <acronym>_WS.asmx)"],"ScopeReason":"The 34 COVERABLE families are provable from the public WSDL (HTTP 200, credential-free, 5.9 MB, 277 ops, 434 DataObjectType schemas confirmed across two independent live instances). Customer-specific queries, Higher Logic partner stored procedures, and custom extension WSDL files are runtime-Discovered at connection time via GetQueryDefinition/ExecuteMethod introspection — not declared as static metadata because their presence, names, and schemas vary per customer installation. MemberDirectory ops (WEBMemberDirectorySearch, WEBMemberDirectoryOrganizationSearch) return Individual/Organization subsets and are classified under those entities rather than as a separate IO.","CustomObjectMarkerPattern":"null — xWeb does not expose a machine-readable custom-object marker. Custom objects and views installed via iWeb/DBA are discoverable only via GetQueryDefinition at runtime. No naming convention is enforced for custom objects.","CustomFieldMarkerPattern":"null — Custom fields in a facade object are returned alongside standard fields from GetFacadeObject/GetQuery. The XSD schema from GetFacadeXMLSchema reveals custom fields at runtime but there is no credential-free marker pattern. Custom fields may follow installation-specific naming conventions.","WSDLOperationCounts":{"totalUniqueOperations":277,"totalComplexTypes":526,"dataObjectTypeSchemas":434,"dataObjectTypeRootGroups":24,"coverableLeaves":34,"informationalLeaves":9,"wsdlSizeBytes":5944192,"provenance":"See Configuration.DeclaredAgainst for the source URLs, fetch date and freshness gaps these counts were measured from."},"DeclaredAgainst":{"wsdlPrimary":{"url":"https://myasm.asm.org/xweb/secure/netforumxml.asmx?WSDL","accessedAt":"2026-06-20","sizeBytes":5944192,"sha256":null,"sha256Gap":"NOT CAPTURED at fetch time. Without it a refetch cannot be diffed against the WSDL this catalog was actually declared from, so ''unchanged since 2026-06-20'' is unprovable. The only comparable is totalUniqueOperations (277) — a bare count that can collide across genuinely different WSDLs (an op removed and another added nets to zero). Capture a sha256 on the next refetch and fill this in; treat the absence as a known blind spot, not as evidence of stability."},"wsdlCrossVerified":{"url":"https://apconetforum.org/xweb/secure/netFORUMXML.asmx?WSDL","accessedAt":"2026-06-20","sha256":null,"role":"A second, independent tenant instance. Used to confirm the SOAP namespace and the endpoint path shape are vendor-wide rather than site-local — NOT to establish the object catalog, which comes from the primary WSDL."},"docSites":["https://documentation.abila.com/netforum-enterprise/2017.1/Content/xWeb/XWeb_Overview.htm","https://documentation.abila.com/netforum-enterprise/2017.1/Content/xWeb/Methods/GetQuery.htm"],"docSetVersion":"Abila netFORUM Enterprise 2017.1","docSitesFetchedAt":null,"docSitesGap":"The Abila doc pages are cited throughout this Configuration (GetQuery @TOP semantics, the DataGrid row-limit behaviour, xWeb overview) but were never date-stamped — only the WSDL got an accessedAt. Any claim sourced to those pages therefore has no freshness evidence behind it.","tenantReleaseVersion":null,"versionSkewGap":"UNRESOLVED AND LOAD-BEARING. The declared catalog is derived from two LIVE tenant WSDLs whose netFORUM release version is unknown and not discoverable without credentials, while the prose evidence is the 2017.1 doc set. Nothing here pins a product version, so a later ''missing'' object CANNOT be attributed: it may mean the catalog is wrong, or that the tenant runs an older release than myasm.asm.org did on 2026-06-20. Contrast Platform/WordPress, which pins wp 7.1 / woocommerce 11.0.1 with zip sha256s precisely so that attribution stays possible.","catalogLastEditedAt":"2026-09-15","catalogLastEditedNote":"migrations/V202607280915__netforum-enterprise__WritablePK.sql withdrew write from five field-less placeholder objects. That edit was reasoned from the SAME 2026-06-20 WSDL read — no refetch occurred — so the accessedAt pin above still describes the evidence base. This field exists because ''source fetched'' and ''catalog edited'' are different dates: without both, a reader cannot tell whether a post-pin edit was evidence-backed or freehand.","note":"Freshness record for the DECLARED object catalog. Distinct from the repo-wide A9 check (scripts/check-catalog-freshness.mjs), which compares package version to git tag and says nothing about whether the vendor surface still looks like this."}}'
WHERE "ID" = '72D0763D-3EA0-4807-BC96-F9B824505C78';

UPDATE "__mj"."CredentialType"
SET "Description" = 'NetForum Enterprise (Community Brands / Abila) two-step SOAP session-token authentication. The connector POSTs a SOAP Authenticate(userName, password) envelope to BaseURL/xweb/secure/netForumXML.asmx and reads the token from the SOAP response header (<AuthorizationToken><Token>) — the body''s AuthenticateResult holds the namespace URI, not the token; every subsequent xWeb call carries that token in a SOAP <AuthorizationToken><Token> header element — NOT HTTP Basic, and NOT an Authorization: Bearer header. BaseURL is per-tenant — required for any operation.'
WHERE "ID" = '078D99D8-22CE-4BF8-9746-128E07799A75';

